# BANYU curated ArduSub parameters. Loaded into SITL by sitl_mavros.launch.py; on the real
# Pixhawk load it once in QGroundControl (docs/por/README.md). The VISO_* and EK3_SRC2_* lines
# are what nogps_odom_beacon needs on the robot; the DVL notes below apply to the sim only.
# Values mirror the working auto-dumped defaults in mav.parm (same names/types).
# BlueROV2 Heavy frame (vectored 6DOF: 8 thrusters).
FRAME_CONFIG 2
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.6
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.15
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.6
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.15

# Mission speeds (m/s).
WP_SPD 1.0
WP_SPD_UP 2.5
WP_SPD_DN 1.5
# Hold current heading in GUIDED/AUTO unless explicitly commanded.
# Default (4 = CORRECT_XTRACK) computes bearing of a zero-length stopping-point
# vector on GUIDED entry, which slews yaw toward 0 deg NED (North = +90 deg ENU).
WP_YAW_BEHAVIOR 0

# Thruster output cap: the ESC power board cannot supply full thruster current.
# AP_Motors6DOF::calc_thrust_to_pwm maps every motor's thrust (-1..1) to
# 1500 +/- (PWM_MAX-1500 | 1500-PWM_MIN), so this range caps all motors in every
# mode: RC MANUAL, ALT_HOLD RC override (POR) and GUIDED velocity (Task 2).
# Full range is 1100..1900 (+/-400 us). Keep the range symmetric around 1500:
#   50% -> 1300 1700   60% -> 1260 1740   70% -> 1220 1780
# Electrical power falls faster than the PWM percentage; raise only after
# measuring board current. QGC Motor Test writes raw PWM and bypasses this cap.
# tools/scripts/check_thrust_limit.py verifies the Pixhawk against these lines.
MOT_PWM_MIN 1300
MOT_PWM_MAX 1700

# Manual/teleop speeds (cm/s).
PILOT_SPEED 200
PILOT_SPEED_UP 100
PILOT_SPEED_DN 0

# Telemetry stream rates (5 Hz for EXTRA1: ESTIMATOR_STATUS and AHRS2 to MAVROS)
SR0_EXTRA1 5
SR1_EXTRA1 5

# EKF failsafe: 0 = never failsafe (keep teleop control authority).
FS_EKF_ACTION 0

# GCS failsafe: 0 = Disabled.
# A tetherless AUV intentionally loses wireless/GCS link to dock when submerged.
# Mission abort and failure fallback to SURFACE is managed onboard by banyu_mission.
FS_GCS_ENABLE 0

# --- Navigation sources: GPS on the surface, DVL underwater ---
# Names/values verified against libraries/AP_VisualOdom/AP_VisualOdom.cpp and
# libraries/AP_NavEKF/AP_NavEKF_Source.h. Overview: banyu_bringup/README.md.
#
# EKF3 carries three switchable source sets. We use two:
#   SRC1 = surface: GPS position + velocity.
#   SRC2 = dive:    DVL body-frame velocity, no absolute position.
# ekf_source_switch.py flips between them on depth, via
# MAV_CMD_SET_EKF_SOURCE_SET. Nothing in ArduPilot switches on depth by itself.
#
# Order matters: setOrigin() rejects a second origin (AP_NavEKF3_Control.cpp:698),
# so a surface GPS fix anchors the EKF origin once, and the DVL then dead-reckons
# from a georeferenced point rather than from nowhere.
#
# The only chain that bootstraps EKF3 aiding from a DVL alone is
#   VISION_POSITION_DELTA -> writeBodyFrameOdom() -> readyToUseBodyOdm() -> AID_RELATIVE
# VISION_SPEED_ESTIMATE / ODOMETRY-twist reach writeExtNavVelData(), which is in
# neither AID_NONE exit branch (AP_NavEKF3_Control.cpp:284-299).

VISO_TYPE 1             # 1 = MAVLink (0:None 2:IntelT265 3:VOXL)

# Lever arm to the sensor, in ArduPilot body frame (FRD: x fwd, y right, z DOWN).
# From bluerov2_gz/models/bluerov2_heavy/model.xacro (dvl_x/dvl_y/dvl_z).
# dvl_z is -0.10 there because Gazebo's model frame is z-UP; below the hull is
# therefore +0.10 here. The DVL model's link origin is the beam-axis
# intersection point, so these transfer with no arithmetic.
VISO_POS_X 0.0
VISO_POS_Y 0.0
VISO_POS_Z 0.10
# 0 = Forward/none. NOT 25 (Down), even though the sensor faces down:
# handle_vision_position_delta_msg() rotates BOTH angle_delta and position_delta
# by this (AP_VisualOdom_Backend.cpp:48-52), and dvl_mavlink_bridge.py already
# emits vehicle-frame FRD. Setting 25 here would rotate correct data into
# nonsense. VISO_ORIENT describes an un-converted sensor's mounting; ours is
# pre-converted.
VISO_ORIENT 0

# Tuning knobs. DELAY_MS is the sensor-to-autopilot latency; the sim's DVL runs
# at 10 Hz so 10 ms is a placeholder, not a measurement.
VISO_DELAY_MS 10
VISO_VEL_M_NSE 0.1

# SRC1 (surface) is deliberately absent from this file: ArduPilot's shipped
# defaults already ARE the surface configuration --
#   EK3_SRC1_POSXY 3 (GPS)   EK3_SRC1_VELXY 3 (GPS)   EK3_SRC1_VELZ 3 (GPS)
#   EK3_SRC1_POSZ  1 (BARO)  EK3_SRC1_YAW   1 (COMPASS)
# (AP_NavEKF_Source.cpp:32-60). Do not re-add them as no-ops.

# SRC2 (dive). Written out in full even where it matches the default: a source
# set is read as a unit, and a half-specified nav config is how you get a
# surprise at depth.
#
# 6 = EXTNAV. readyToUseBodyOdm() returns false unless VELXY is EXTNAV or
# WHEEL_ENCODER, so this line is what actually lets the DVL aid the filter.
EK3_SRC2_VELXY 6
# No horizontal position source. A DVL gives velocity, not absolute position;
# GPS(3) here would make EKF3 wait at depth for a fix it cannot have.
# 0 = NONE. Aiding then comes from readyToUseBodyOdm() -> AID_RELATIVE.
EK3_SRC2_POSXY 0
# Depth from the barometer, which a sub genuinely has. (Default, restated.)
EK3_SRC2_POSZ 1
# Vertical velocity is derived from the baro, not from the DVL: the bridge sends
# VISION_POSITION_DELTA, which reaches writeBodyFrameOdom(), not the ExtNav
# velocity path EXTNAV(6) here would select. (Default, restated.)
EK3_SRC2_VELZ 0
# Compass, NOT the SRC2 default of 0/NONE. With no yaw source EKF3 never
# completes yaw alignment and aiding is blocked outright -- the DVL would look
# dead at depth for a reason that has nothing to do with the DVL.
EK3_SRC2_YAW 1

# --- Note on SITL's synthetic GPS ---
# SITL synthesises a GPS from Gazebo ground truth (SITL.cpp:725 declares the
# GPS1_ subgroup, SIM_GPS.cpp:42 the ENABLE member) and it does NOT cut out when
# the vehicle submerges. It is left ENABLED (the default) so the surface half of
# the architecture is testable at all; SIM_GPS1_ENABLE 0 was the right setting
# only while SRC1 itself was the DVL.
#
# The catch: because sim GPS keeps streaming at depth, "EKF3 is healthy
# underwater" proves nothing on its own. What proves it is the source SET being
# SRC2, where POSXY is NONE -- so POS_HORIZ_ABS must go clear and POS_HORIZ_REL
# set. Ground truth leaking in would keep POS_HORIZ_ABS set. See the README.
